    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15590" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ē-mātūresco</span></b> ,
			rŭi, 3, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. inch. n.</i>, <i>to grow
				quite ripe</i>, <i>to come to maturity</i> (very
			rare). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">semen,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					25, 4, 17, § 36</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">segetes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					2, 29, 7</span></i>
			.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>to grow softer</i>,
				<i>be mitigated</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ira Caesaris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Tr. 2, 124</span></i>
			.</div>
